---
title: "Studio Row Selection Test"
---

This is an internal page used to check the row selection behaviours that the grid enables only when it is running inside AG Studio. It is intentionally left out of the site navigation.

Each behaviour sits behind an internal feature flag rather than a grid option. Every grid created inside Studio has them on automatically, so each example here turns its flag on with `_createInternalFeatureFlagsModule` instead.

## Single row selection

Clicking a row selects it, and clicking it again deselects it — where by default a click on the selected row does nothing.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Toggle Selection Single" name="toggle-selection-single" /%}

## Multi row selection

The same toggle, but only when the clicked row is the whole selection. {% kbd "^ Ctrl" /%}-click a second row first to check that the next click reduces the selection to the clicked row rather than deselecting it.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Toggle Selection Multi" name="toggle-selection-multi" /%}

## Grouped rows

With `groupSelects: 'descendants'`, clicking a selected group deselects it and its descendants, as long as nothing outside that subtree is selected. {% kbd "^ Ctrl" /%}-click a second country to check that the click reduces the selection to one country instead.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Toggle Group Selection" name="toggle-group-selection" /%}

## Space follows click selection

{% kbd "␣ Space" /%} on a focused row obeys `enableClickSelection` as a click does, so with `false` it neither selects nor deselects the row. {% kbd "␣ Space" /%} on the checkbox cell still toggles the row, as clicking the checkbox does. Change the dropdown to check that `'enableSelection'` lets {% kbd "␣ Space" /%} select but not deselect, and `'enableDeselection'` the reverse.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Space Follows Click Selection" name="space-key-follows-click-selection" /%}
